  "notes": "Official blank SBA Form 413 (05-24) template. Verified directly against the PDF's AcroForm widgets (fitz page.widgets()): 21 of 25 fields are genuinely empty form fields (field_value=''), so a correct extraction returns null for those, not an echo of the printed label (same failure mode documented for CMS-1500 and SBA Form 1919). Exactly 4 widgets carry a non-empty default -- 'TotalAssets' (x2, one per column), 'TotalLiabilities', 'Net Worth' -- all literally '0', baked into the template by SBA, not filled in by an applicant. So total_assets/total_liabilities/net_worth expect 0 (found), not null. contingent_liabilities' 4 sub-line widgets (As Endorser or Co-Maker, Legal Claims and Judgements, Provision for Federal Income Tax, Other Special Debt) are all genuinely blank -- expects null. An earlier version of this gold file had this backwards (expected null for the totals, expected 0 for contingent_liabilities), based on a misreading of get_text()'s flattened '$ 0' lines without checking which widgets they actually belonged to -- corrected after inspecting page.widgets() directly."
